Afficher moins
Subject: [PATCH] Fix back navigation: replace ad-hoc returnTo logic with a
 history stack
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
- Add navHistory[] to appState for tracking navigation depth
- Add pushNavHistory(), goBack(), _restoreScreenById() to router.js
  so all back navigation flows through one correct, consistent path
- Fix the root cause of "goes to profile randomly": navigateTo() was
  used with unknown section names (e.g. 'skill-library', 'all-goals')
  which silently fell through to routes.profile()
- Fix bottom-nav highlight not updating when returning to screen IDs
  that were handled via showScreen() directly
- All back buttons in detail screens now call goBack() rather than
  closeSession/SkillDetail with a baked-in returnTo string
- navigateTo() clears navHistory so bottom-nav jumps reset context
- Add initSwipeBack(): right-swipe from left screen edge (≤30px)
  triggers goBack(); includes direction-lock to avoid conflicts with
  vertical scrolling, and guards against .swipe-row card elements
- deleteSession() no longer takes a returnTo param; calls goBack()
- showSkillDetail/KnowledgePage guard against re-pushing history when
  re-rendering the screen they're already on
